== Title decisions ==

* '''[[Generalization]] → [[Generalization (machine learning)]]''' because unqualified generalization has durable meanings in logic, psychology, linguistics, mathematics, and ordinary reasoning.
* '''[[Data leakage]] → [[Data leakage (machine learning)]]''' because unqualified data leakage also names information-security/privacy disclosure and exfiltration.
* [[Spurious correlation]] remains unqualified because the statistical concept is broader than machine learning and is useful across science, causal inference, and prediction.
* [[Distribution shift]] remains unqualified because it already denotes the statistical mismatch between source/training and target/deployment distributions and is not specific to one model family.
* [[Benchmark contamination]] remains unqualified; its Core scope must cover evaluation contamination generally, while noting its recent prominence in large-model benchmarks.
* Informal '''“fitting bias”''' is rejected as a canonical umbrella. Existing established concepts already separate underfitting, overfitting, inductive bias, estimator bias, and model-selection bias.

== Domain decision ==

No new controlled Domain is required.

Primary Domain is '''Computer science''', with substantive cross-domain use of Mathematics, Science, and Cognitive science only where justified.

No “Machine learning” Domain is introduced.

