== Source-family audit ==

* '''statistical learning texts''' — generalization, overfitting, underfitting, inductive bias, dataset roles.
* '''Belkin et al. (2019)''' — double descent and limits of simplistic classical complexity curves.
* '''Cawley & Talbot (2010), JMLR''' — overfitting in model selection and selection bias in performance evaluation.
* '''Quiñonero-Candela et al., Dataset Shift in Machine Learning''' — distribution/dataset/covariate shift.
* '''Kaufman et al. (2012)''' — leakage in data mining / predictive modeling.
* '''Geirhos et al. (2020), Nature Machine Intelligence''' — shortcut learning.
* '''PMLR/AISTATS/ICML recent spurious-correlation work''' — modern treatment of spurious features and OOD generalization.
* '''contamination-detection / live-benchmark literature''' — benchmark contamination, used as current examples rather than the full definition.
* '''current 2026 machine-learning texts''' — overfitting/underfitting and model-selection framing.

